  Excellent point.  Not just another wish, but a wish much better suited
to your current emergency.  Wishing way in advance means you don't know
what you'll need.  (Cue story of player on Astral who only managed to
Ascend by wishing for a magic whistle.)  I'll also note that early
wishes seem to guarantee imminent death.  Even an early blessed (0:3)
wand of wishing won't guarantee a full kit.

  So the player is going to have to play carefully and tactically while
exploring no matter what.  Carrying a lit magic lamp greatly improves
careful tactical play.  Not only because it's light, but because the
improvement doesn't require extra effort/thinking on the player's part.
It smooths out the game.  (One of the many ways NetHack kills players is
by frequent context shifts until the player kamikaze attacks out of
sheer frustration.)  (The only class that might ignore this advice is
Monk, as the Eyes of the Overworld are the Monk Quest Artifact.)
 

  (Something else frequently ignored with wishes is that they're not
guaranteed.  Low enough luck means "Unfortunately nothing happens."  I
learned that the hard way.  So for a really effective wish a player must
not only know in advance what the emergency will be, but the current
state of their luck.  A lot of players seem barely aware that in-game
luck exists.)

  With the magic lamp the player has banished darkness from the rest of
the game.  Remember, it's not just ranged attacks and tactical
maneuvering where light helps.  Exploring is greatly helped by light as
well.


